nak: QMD dependency field setters, Ampere B to Blackwell B

NVIDIA's driver (libnvidia-eglcore.so 615.78.08) orders compute work with QMD dependencies:
DEPENDENCE_COUNTER, DEPENDENT_QMD{0,1} {ENABLE, ACTION = DECREMENT_DEPENDENCE, PREFETCH,
POINTER} and the per-QMD INVALIDATE_{TEXTURE_DATA,SHADER_DATA,SHADER_CONSTANT}_CACHE bits
(writers E 0xd32f60, E 0xd33340, E 0xd334a0, E 0xd33fb0), plus empty QMDs with CTA 1x1x1 and
grid 0 (E 0xd34709).  Its writers have one arm per QMD layout; it uses them for compute classes
above 0xc6bf outside GA100.  Expose setters for those fields to NVK for NAK's QMD layouts on
those classes: V03_00 (AMPERE_COMPUTE_B, ADA_COMPUTE_A; the second dependent QMD's pointer in
word 9, where the driver stores it, E 0xd335d5), V04_00 (HOPPER_COMPUTE_A) and V05_00
(BLACKWELL_COMPUTE_A/B).  Any other class aborts with a named reason.

